  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 238 PM CDT Fri Oct 23 2026\n\nOn late Monday, the wave will tilt negatively across southeast South \nDakota. Some CAPE is tucked right in the triple point, but the speed \nof the system keeps the warm sector out of the state until the \novernight hours. CAPE will build on the warm sector of the front as \nit stalls across the middle of the state. Much of next week will \nhave split weather between the north and southern half. The northern \nhalf will have more seasonal temperatures whereas 70 degree highs \nwill be common across the south. Rain and some thunderstorms will \nremain in the picture. This pattern will remain until the east CONUS \nridge is broken down by a stronger system from the west.",
